<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Félix María Calleja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1753–<a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Félix María Calleja del Rey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Félix María Calleja was a Spanish army officer who led royalist forces against the Mexican insurgents from 1810. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-hidalgo-y-costilla">Miguel Hidalgo</a>'s much larger army at the Bridge of Calderón in January 1811 and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-morelos">José María Morelos</a> at Cuautla in 1812. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> from 1813 to 1816 he pursued a harsh counter-insurgency that brought the rebellion close to defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felix-maria-calleja.jpg" alt="Félix María Calleja" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Perovani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Virrey_F%C3%A9lix_Mar%C3%ADa_Calleja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
